# Accessibility

- Semantic HTML first; ARIA only when semantics are insufficient.
- One logical `h1` per view; heading levels never skip arbitrarily.
- All interactive elements keyboard reachable with visible **focus** styles (match design system).
- Forms: `<label>` associated with controls; describe errors with `aria-describedby` / live regions when appropriate.
- Dialogs/drawers/menus: focus trap, `aria-modal`, return focus on close; Escape closes when expected.
- Command palette: typeahead, roving tabindex or arrow-key patterns per WAI-ARIA practices.
- Color contrast meets WCAG for text and controls; do not rely on color alone for state.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` for animations and large transitions.
- Test critical flows with keyboard only and screen reader spot-checks for new patterns.
